"""Pick a sample photo (or upload your own) -> detect -> show boxes: object
detection, indah-style.

The model is SSD-MobileNetV1, trained on COCO's 80 object classes, run with
``onnxruntime``. Weights (about 28 MB) download once from the Hugging Face Hub
mirror of the official ONNX Model Zoo and are cached, so a freshly started server
pays that cost once, then detects from RAM - the same lazy-download-and-cache
pattern ``upload_classify.py`` uses for its MobileNetV2 classifier.
``onnxruntime``, Pillow, and ``huggingface_hub`` are this demo's own dependencies,
not indah's, and they're imported lazily inside ``detect`` so the rest of the
module works without any of them installed.

Boxes use ``label_mode="hover"``: with several detections on one image, a
permanent label per box gets noisy fast, so labels show as a tooltip on hover
instead (indah#78). Scroll to zoom into a small detection, drag to pan once
zoomed - both come from ``ImageOverlay`` itself (indah#77), no code here.

A picker of sample photos runs detection immediately on load (no click required)
so a first-time visitor sees the model work before trying their own (the
result-out-of-the-box UX from docs/DEMOS-DOCS-ROUND2.md's A5). The five bundled
here (a cyclist, a parking lot, a living room, after-work drinks, an airport
luggage carousel) are picked because they hold several different COCO classes at
once, which is more interesting for detection than a single clean subject is for
classification. Upload your own and the detector may miss things or mislabel them
- SSD-MobileNetV1 is a small, fast, CPU-friendly model (mAP ~0.23 on COCO), not a
state-of-the-art one; that trade-off is what keeps this demo light enough to
bundle and run per-request on a shared box.

Each viewer gets an isolated session (``session_factory``), so one person's
upload and detections are private to their tab. Runs on Tier 0 (SSE + POST),
so it works behind Colab's proxy.

Run it with:  python examples/object_detection.py
Then open the URL and click a sample, or upload an image. No Node, at install or
at runtime.
"""

import asyncio
import base64

import indah
from indah import (
    Button,
    Card,
    Column,
    ImageOverlay,
    Row,
    Session,
    Signal,
    Spinner,
    Text,
    Upload,
    UploadedFile,
    create_app,
)

